    "id": "8fdfe233-7bdb-4244-acd9-289b82a5aa1d",
    "code": "WO-2026-0042",
    "building_id": "7e7c1500-d9b2-4b43-b7cf-650648816b21",
    "equipment_id": "1d57a018-5585-49b7-b13e-7fd001c44fb8",
    "prediction_id": null,
    "anomaly_id": null,
    "title": "Gen Set 5 Diagnostic Assessment & Baseline Establishment",
    "description": "Phase 41-03/44/46: Establish diagnostic baseline for Gen Set 5 onboarding. Measure fuel system (cavitation detection), speed control (governor hunting), engine condition (knock/temperature), and bearing wear using phyphox accelerometer/audio + manual sensor readings. Validate R611,820.75 repair quote before authorization. 4-year failure pattern: 2023 speed controller fail → 2024 fuel pump leak → 2025 injectors blocked. Post-repair: track effectiveness.",
    "priority": "high",
    "status": "scheduled",
    "scheduled_date": null,
    "scheduled_start": null,
    "scheduled_end": null,
    "estimated_duration_hours": null,
    "assigned_to": "John Smith",
    "assigned_team": "general",
    "started_at": null,
    "completed_at": null,
    "actual_duration_hours": null,
    "labor_cost_zar": null,
    "parts_cost_zar": null,
    "total_cost_zar": null,
    "parts_required": null,
    "parts_used": null,
    "work_performed": null,
    "findings": null,
    "follow_up_required": false,
    "follow_up_notes": "FIELD PROCEDURE: CONDITIONAL ASSESSMENT - S002-GEN-B1-005 (Mitsubishi 1,375 kVA)\nScope: Validate quoted fuel injection pump taper roller bearings and 12x injector plungers.\n\nPHASE 1 - SETUP AND CONFIGURATION\n1) Safety\n- Use double hearing protection (ear plugs + ear muffs).\n- Route and secure sensor and phone cables away from fan, belts, and coupling.\n- Keep clear of hot exhaust and turbo surfaces.\n\n2) Analyzer Configuration\n- Fmax: 5000 Hz\n- Resolution: 3200 lines\n- Measurement: Acceleration (g-Peak)\n- Enable Envelope/Demodulation if available.\n\n3) Operating Condition\n- Run at rated speed (1500 RPM at 50 Hz site, or 1800 RPM at 60 Hz if applicable).\n- Prefer loaded condition at 30-50% minimum.\n\nPHASE 2 - FUEL INJECTION PUMP TEST\n4) Identify and label pumps\n- PUMP_A = Left / Bank 1\n- PUMP_B = Right / Bank 2\n\n5) Pump Drive End (DE) readings\n- Mount at pump housing nearest engine drive.\n- Capture Vertical and Horizontal readings for each pump.\n\n6) Pump Non-Drive End (NDE) readings\n- Mount on rear of pump housing.\n- Capture Axial reading (parallel to shaft) for each pump.\n\n7) Repeat full DE + NDE sequence for PUMP_B.\n\nPHASE 3 - INJECTOR AND PLUNGER TEST\n8) Map cylinders CYL_01 to CYL_12.\n\n9) Sensor placement per cylinder\n- Place magnetic accelerometer on cylinder head bolt nearest injector body.\n- Do not place on exhaust manifold.\n\n10) Data capture per cylinder\n- Record 5-10 second time waveform.\n- Record 10 second audio clip near injector body (if available).\n\n11) Repeat identical mounting method for CYL_02 through CYL_12 for valid comparison.\n\nPHASE 4 - IMMEDIATE FIELD SANITY CHECK\n12) Compare PUMP_A vs PUMP_B g-Peak\n- Example rule: 0.5g vs 2.5g indicates probable pump-side bearing failure.\n- If both are <0.5g, bearing fault evidence is weak at time of test.\n\n13) Compare injector waveform consistency\n- Healthy: sharp consistent spikes across cylinders.\n- Suspect: flat or fuzzy waveform on one cylinder vs peers (possible misfire/plunger wear).\n\nPHASE 5 - DATA PACKAGING AND REPORTING\n14) Save files using system naming convention\n- SITE-002_S002-GEN-B1-005_PUMP_A_DE_V\n- SITE-002_S002-GEN-B1-005_PUMP_A_DE_H\n- SITE-002_S002-GEN-B1-005_PUMP_A_NDE_A\n- SITE-002_S002-GEN-B1-005_PUMP_B_DE_V\n- SITE-002_S002-GEN-B1-005_PUMP_B_DE_H\n- SITE-002_S002-GEN-B1-005_PUMP_B_NDE_A\n- SITE-002_S002-GEN-B1-005_CYL_01_TWF\n- SITE-002_S002-GEN-B1-005_CYL_01_AUDIO\n- Repeat through CYL_12.\n\n15) Capture placement photos\n- Take one photo per measurement location so post-repair comparison is repeatable.\n\nAcceptance objective:\n- Confirm whether quoted blanket replacement is justified by measured pump and cylinder-level evidence.",
